{
  "abstract": "Proves sharp bounds for both extrema of three consecutive ordinary continued-fraction approximation coefficients. Exact finite runs of every integer central digit at least two have rational four-corner constants, unique coordinate extremizers, strict actual inequalities, and optimality within the prescribed digit classes. The project also proves exact clipping on every closed unit-square rectangle for every real parameter at least one; sharp inverse stability for both extrema for every real parameter at least two, including their equality loci and actual-convergent optimality; fixed-word sharpness at a fixed index; constant-future and exhausted-past boundary results; effective two-sided run-gap estimates; optimal actual constant-digit-window cutoffs; and an executable rational Lean interface.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "JD Jones"
    }
  ],
